{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>A psalm of David. YHWH is my shepherd; I shall not lack.</b> This psalm is precious, and he likened himself to a sheep whose trust rests upon the shepherd. And HaShem is the one who shepherds me; therefore I shall lack nothing at all. The sense: it shall not be lacking to me — that which I need, in the manner of [the verse] 'and there is no lack' [Psalm 34:11]."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:28:20.503785698Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}